--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Measurement records — CC BY 4.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Applies to: results_v2/ (all per-sample edit records, attention records,
derived metrics, the decoder audit, and results_v2/superseded/).

These are measurements we produced by running the models listed below. They are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The records contain edited chain-of-thought text derived from the ECoT
reasoning annotations (MIT). They contain no images and no raw demonstration
trajectories from any upstream corpus.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Third-party material — NOT relicensed by this release
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
This benchmark evaluates and depends on material owned by others. Using it
requires complying with their terms directly. Nothing above grants any right
to the following.

Every line in this section was read from the Hugging Face Hub API rather than
written from memory, by scripts/fetch_upstream_licenses.py. The machine-readable
record, including each repo's resolved commit sha, is
results_v2/license_report.json, and scripts/verify_paper_numbers.py asserts
that this file agrees with it. Where the Hub declares no license we say so
instead of assigning one.

Evaluation corpora (accessed at run time; not redistributed here):
  openvla/modified_libero_rlds ................. MIT
      LIBERO-90 observations; the primary P1/P2 suite.
  Embodied-CoT/embodied_features_and_demos_libero  MIT
      LIBERO CoT reasoning annotations. Our released edited-CoT strings are
      DERIVATIVE of this corpus; MIT is what permits us to release them.
  IPEC-COMMUNITY/bridge_orig_lerobot ........... Apache-2.0
  IPEC-COMMUNITY/fractal20220817_data_lerobot .. Apache-2.0
  IPEC-COMMUNITY/bc_z_lerobot .................. Apache-2.0
      The three cross-corpus sweeps (Bridge V2, RT-1/Fractal, BC-Z at N=30
      each) load these LeRobot re-hosts, so Apache-2.0 is the license that
      governs our use. It is not necessarily the license of the original
      corpus, and if you obtain Bridge V2 or BC-Z from their primary sources
      instead you are under those sources' terms, not these.
  Embodied-CoT/embodied_features_bridge ........ MIT
      Bridge CoT annotations, referenced by the F4-deconfound subset training
      that ships as scaffolding. No reported number depends on it.

Model checkpoints (downloaded from Hugging Face at run time):
  openvla/openvla-7b ........................................... MIT
  openvla/openvla-7b-finetuned-libero-{spatial,object,goal,10} .. MIT
  Embodied-CoT/ecot-openvla-7b-bridge .......................... MIT
  yinchenghust/deepthinkvla_{base,libero_cot_sft,libero_cot_rl}
      NO LICENSE DECLARED UPSTREAM. As of the date of this release these three
      model repos carry no license tag, no cardData license, and no license
      file on the Hub. We therefore state no license for them rather than guess
      one, and we grant none. They are PaliGemma derivatives, so the Google
      Gemma Terms of Use apply to the base model regardless:
      https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms
      Practical consequence: only attention records exist for these three
      rows, and if you need a license for redistribution you must obtain one
      from the upstream authors.

Our 7 LoRA fine-tunes are derivatives of Embodied-CoT/ecot-openvla-7b-bridge
(MIT) — the base every training config sets — and are released under the MIT
terms in section 1.

Software dependencies (transformers, torch, LIBERO, robosuite, MuJoCo, TFDS,
and others in requirements.txt) carry their own licenses.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
If you use CoT-Faith, please cite the paper and also cite the upstream corpora
and checkpoints you evaluate on. The faithfulness numbers are not meaningful
without knowing which model and corpus produced them, so the attribution is
substantive rather than a formality.
